description:
Represent metric availability with an explicit reason, not one overloaded null.

At minimum distinguish:

- no reviewed scope;
- reviewed scope but no successfully processed scope;
- processed scope with zero predictions;
- layer migration incomplete or below readiness threshold;
- unscorable findings lacking required provenance;
- computable numeric result.

For precision, an empty processed prediction denominator is not the same condition as absent or unread scope, even when neither produces a numeric fraction. Markdown and JSON must retain the state and all denominator counts.

Legacy data flows may use migration-incomplete in readiness reports. Baseline series 1 itself is blocked until the four-layer readiness gate passes; it does not publish an unscorable flow layer as though that were a baseline result.
